  "<section class=\"course-page\" id=\"lesson-04\" data-chapter11-complete=\"resting-potential\" hidden=\"\">\n<div class=\"p2-topic\">\n<header class=\"page-header\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-114\">Learn \u00b7 Chapter 11</p>\n<h1 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-115\">The resting neuron</h1>\n<p class=\"lesson-question\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-116\">What is happening at the membrane before a neuron fires?</p>\n<div class=\"goal-strip\"><div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-01\">Learning goal</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-02\">I can explain the resting potential and the roles of leak channels and the sodium-potassium pump.</p></div>\n<div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-03\">Before you begin</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-04\">Review the axon and cell membrane. This lesson introduces the ions and their movements.</p></div></div>\n<details class=\"page-guide\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-guide-summary\"><strong>How to complete this lesson</strong> \u2014 Learn \u2192 practise \u2192 required check \u2192 finish</summary>\n<div>\n<ol>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-guide-01\"><strong>Start with the lesson.</strong> Read the learning goal and \u201cBefore you begin,\u201d then work through the explanation, diagrams and examples below. The embedded textbook is optional support: open it when you want another explanation or a closer look at a figure.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-guide-02\"><strong>Use the learning goal and starting reminder.</strong> The learning goal above tells you what you must be able to explain. Read \u201cBefore you begin\u201d next to connect this lesson to what you already know.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-guide-03\"><strong>Work through the online lesson in order.</strong> Read each teaching section and study its diagrams, examples and comparisons. Select an underlined biology term when you need its meaning. Use the video or Vocabulary help when an idea is still unclear.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-guide-04\"><strong>Complete the required chapter check.</strong> Open the check near the bottom and select Start. For multiple choice, select Check answer; a correct answer unlocks the related writing. Answer in your own words and select Save written response for every response box.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-guide-05\"><strong>Submit only when the required work is complete.</strong> Check that every required item has been attempted and every written response is saved. Then select Submit and finish. This stops the timer, records the completed run in All My Work and updates chapter progress.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-guide-06\"><strong>Use optional practice only when it helps.</strong> Optional source practice and Practice &amp; Review activities can help you study, but they do not count toward the 12 required chapter checks.</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-guide-07\"><strong>Expected work:</strong> complete the lesson and submit the required chapter check. Use optional reading, videos and practice when they help. Drafts save automatically as you work in this browser.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n<div class=\"textbook-band\"><div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-05\">Optional embedded reading</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-06\"><strong>Chapter 11 \u00b7 pp. 374\u2013375</strong></p></div><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"15\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-07\">Open at p. 374</a></div>\n<p class=\"lesson-term-strip\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-teacher-voice-terms\"><strong>Key terms:</strong> resting membrane potential \u00b7 Na\u207a \u00b7 K\u207a \u00b7 potassium leak channel \u00b7 sodium-potassium pump \u00b7 selective permeability</p>\n<details class=\"lesson-vocabulary-help\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-teacher-voice-vocab-summary\">Vocabulary help</summary>\n<section class=\"lesson-words\" aria-labelledby=\"lesson-04-anchor-words\"><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-08\">Key terms</p><h2 id=\"lesson-04-anchor-words\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-09\">Words for this lesson</h2><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-10\">Use these definitions when you need help with a term.</p><dl>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"resting membrane potential\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-04\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-11\">resting membrane potential</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-12\">the voltage difference across a resting neuron\u2019s membrane</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"selective permeability\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-04\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-13\">selective permeability</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-14\">allowing some substances across a membrane more easily than others</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"depolarization\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-04\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-15\">depolarization</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-16\">the inside of the membrane becoming less negative</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"repolarization\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-04\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-17\">repolarization</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-18\">the membrane voltage returning toward its resting level</dd></div>\n</dl></section>\n<details class=\"lesson-term-inventory\"><summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-19\">More vocabulary for this lesson</summary><div><section aria-labelledby=\"lesson-04-all-terms\"><h3 id=\"lesson-04-all-terms\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-20\">Lesson vocabulary</h3><dl><div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-21\">resting membrane potential \u00b7 ion gradient \u00b7 selective permeability \u00b7 axon \u00b7 neuron \u00b7 depolarization \u00b7 repolarization \u00b7 refractory period</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l04-setup-22\">Select an underlined term for its definition. Your vocabulary writing is saved in Process Collection.</dd></div></dl></section></div></details>\n</details>\n</header>\n",
